## Becket Git Branch Naming Convention (MDC Rules)

Purpose: Keep branch names predictable, searchable, and aligned with UI library work in this monorepo.

Applies to all branches created for pull requests into `main`.

---

## Branch format

Use this format:

`<type>/<scope>/<short-description>`

Rules:
- Use lowercase only.
- Use hyphens (`-`) between words.
- Do not use spaces, underscores, or special characters.
- Keep the description concise and action-oriented.

---

## Allowed branch types

- `feat` - New component, variant, token, or capability.
- `fix` - Bug fix or regression fix.
- `refactor` - Internal code change with no intended behavior change.
- `docs` - Documentation and Storybook docs-only updates.
- `test` - Tests only.
- `chore` - Tooling, dependency, or maintenance work.
- `build` - Build/release/configuration pipeline changes.
- `ci` - CI workflow and automation updates.

---

## Scope guidance (UI library)

Scope should identify the main area affected:
- Component scope: `button`, `heading`, `flex`, `stack`
- Package scope: `react`, `tokens`, `docs`
- Infra scope: `storybook`, `turbo`, `release`

If multiple areas are touched, use the dominant area (`react` or `tokens`) instead of listing many scopes.

---

## Examples

Valid:
- `feat/heading/add-size-variants`
- `feat/button/add-loading-state`
- `fix/flex/gradient-border-overflow`
- `fix/tokens/missing-semantic-color`
- `docs/storybook/improve-button-usage`
- `chore/react/update-storybook-deps`
- `ci/release/add-pr-checks`

Invalid:
- `feature/Heading/new-styles` (wrong type + uppercase scope)
- `fix/short-description` (missing scope)
- `feat/button/add_new_styles` (underscore)
- `feat/button/` (missing description)

---

## Optional ticket integration

When using task IDs, append them at the end of scope or start of description:
- `feat/button/1234-add-loading-state`
- `fix/tokens/jira-482-missing-color-token`

Keep the same lowercase + hyphen rules.

---

## Workflow expectations

- Create short-lived topic branches from `main`.
- Open PRs early and keep them focused on one concern.
- Delete merged branches to keep the repo clean.

This convention is the default for Becket contributions unless a release or hotfix process requires a temporary exception.
